From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:54:44 +0800
Subject: backend-anland: bridge clipboard and text input

Bridge Weston selections to Anland with bounded asynchronous pipe reads
and publish Android clipboard updates through a backend-owned data
source. Keep the transfer off the compositor's blocking paths, cap
clipboard contents at 1 MiB, and cache synchronized text to suppress
feedback loops and restore it after consumer reconnects.

Register a narrow text-backend plugin API and use it to commit validated
UTF-8 to the active text-input-v1 client. Apply the same payload limits
to incoming text and use timeout-bounded nonblocking sends for
data-channel output events.
